# SYNTHETIC. Written from the greeting porter's SMTP relay gives an app (porter-proxy,
# `220 porter ESMTP ready`, then an EHLO reply that offers no AUTH and no STARTTLS): the relay
# signed in to the real server before the app saw a byte, so the session goes from EHLO to MAIL.

S: 220 porter ESMTP ready
C: EHLO client.example
S: 250-porter
S: 250-SIZE 35882577
S: 250-8BITMIME
S: 250 PIPELINING
C: MAIL FROM:<ada@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.0 OK
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.5 OK
C: DATA
S: 354 End data with <CR><LF>.<CR><LF>
C: Subject: hi
C:
C: hi
C: .
S: 250 2.0.0 OK queued
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
DONE
